Third-party notices: torch_scatter 2.1.2 public-interface adaptation
========================================================================

Upstream API source: https://github.com/rusty1s/pytorch_scatter/blob/2.1.2/torch_scatter/segment_coo.py
Version: 2.1.2
Attribution scope: python/ops_gnn/segment_coo.py

The adapted material is the public Python interface declarations for
segment_sum_coo, segment_add_coo, segment_mean_coo, segment_min_coo,
segment_max_coo, and segment_coo: function names, parameter names/order,
type annotations, default values, and return annotations. The sum/add/mean
dispatch in segment_coo also retains the upstream public reduction mapping
and calls to segment_sum_coo / segment_mean_coo, with rewritten conditions.

The wrapper bodies use this project's _pybind.segment_coo_forward and
SEGMENT_COO_* constants instead of upstream torch.ops.torch_scatter calls.
The add wrapper delegates to this project's sum wrapper; min/max dispatch
uses this project's values-only binding. Current docstrings describe this
project's output-buffer, integer-mean and tie-breaking behavior; they do
not include the upstream long-form segment_coo docstring, examples or image.
This attribution does not describe the Ascend host/kernel or independent
PyTorch test reference as copied upstream CPU/CUDA implementations.

